cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper it accompanies."
title: "XAI_Rfpipe: reproducible pipeline for explainable neural forecasting of rainfall-distribution shifts"
abstract: >-
  End-to-end pipeline reproducing every experiment, statistical test, table and
  result figure in "Best of how many? Candidate-count bias in environmental
  model benchmarking": divergence-target construction from daily reanalysis, a
  model-family comparison under chronological splits, and the resolvability
  audit - a candidate-aware reference null for family win counts, a
  randomisation test by common relabelling of model identities, a prospective
  design report, pool-sensitivity analysis, and a simulation study bounding
  where the reference null holds and where it fails.
type: software
license: MIT
